# pair-mds-gwes v0.1.1

A pip-installable redesign of the previous `pair_logistic_mds` fixed-MDS path.

This version keeps useful parts of the old script:

- tree-MDS correction;
- response-wise null model caching;
- fast logistic score testing;
- optional exact logistic LRT with Firth fallback;
- compact bidirectional pair output.

It removes the old failed parts from the main model:

- no GRM random effect;
- no GLMM/LMM;
- no response-specific `sigma2_g`/`tau`;
- no local-distance filtering;
- no classification tiers.

## Model

For each PAN-GWES/SpydrPick candidate pair `(u, v)`, both directions are tested:

```text
logit(P(v = 1)) = alpha + beta*u + MDS1 + ... + MDSk
logit(P(u = 1)) = alpha + beta*v + MDS1 + ... + MDSk
```

The pair-level score is:

```text
bidirectional_score = min(-log10(p_u_to_v), -log10(p_v_to_u))
```

## Installation

From the unzipped directory:

```bash
pip install .
```

or editable mode:

```bash
pip install -e .
```

## Usage

With a Newick tree:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes \
  --fasta fake.fa \
  --pairs pairs.tsv \
  --tree tree.nwk \
  --n-mds 10 \
  --out results \
  --overwrite
```

Without a tree, the tool builds a sample Hamming distance matrix from the fake FASTA and uses MDS:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes \
  --fasta fake.fa \
  --pairs pairs.tsv \
  --n-mds 10 \
  --out results \
  --overwrite
```

Optional SPA-style p-values for the score test:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes \
  --fasta fake.fa \
  --pairs pairs.tsv \
  --tree tree.nwk \
  --spa \
  --out results_spa \
  --overwrite
```

Optional exact logistic LRT with Firth fallback:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes \
  --fasta fake.fa \
  --pairs pairs.tsv \
  --tree tree.nwk \
  --engine exact \
  --out results_exact \
  --overwrite
```

## Pair file

If the pair file has no header, columns are interpreted as:

```text
u v distance ARACNE MI count M2 min_distance max_distance ...
```

Only `u` and `v` are required. The compact output preserves `distance`, `min_distance`, and `MI` if present.

## Main output

`pair_mds_logistic.tsv` has minimized columns:

```text
u
v
distance       # if present
min_distance   # if present
MI             # if present
n11
n10
n01
n00
r2
or
p_u_to_v
p_v_to_u
bidirectional_score
status
```

Audit files:

```text
mds_covariates.tsv
mds_summary.tsv
null_logistic_summary.tsv
run_summary.txt
```

## Method note

This tool estimates structure-conditioned candidate pangenome covariation. It asks whether candidate locus pairs remain associated after broad tree- or FASTA-distance-MDS correction, without using a flexible GRM random effect that can absorb fitness-driven epistatic signals as population structure.


## Plotting

A command-line plotter is installed as `pair-mds-gwes-plot`. The raw R script is still included for audit:

```bash
Rscript scripts/plot_pair_mds_gwes.R \
  --input results/pair_mds_logistic.tsv \
  --out results/pair_distance_score.png
```

Default x-axis is `distance` if present; otherwise the script uses `abs(v - u)`.
Default y-axis is `bidirectional_score`.

Highlight a known pair:

```bash
Rscript scripts/plot_pair_mds_gwes.R \
  --input results/pair_mds_logistic.tsv \
  --out results/pair_distance_score.png \
  --highlight-pair 50000,90000 \
  --threshold 5
```

Write top hits:

```bash
Rscript scripts/plot_pair_mds_gwes.R \
  --input results/pair_mds_logistic.tsv \
  --out results/pair_distance_score.png \
  --top-out results/top_pairs.tsv \
  --top-n 100
```

R dependencies:

```r
install.packages(c("ggplot2", "data.table"))
```


## Progress tracking and logs

`pair-mds-gwes` now prints internal progress messages to stderr, including major steps, null-model progress, pair-scan progress, rate, and status counts.

Example messages:

```text
[pair-mds-gwes] step=6/7_scan_pairs elapsed=12.4s start pairs=100000 min_count=3
[2026-06-11 14:00:00] null_models_progress=500/2500 ( 20.0%) elapsed=4.1s rate=122.0/s ok=500 fail=0
[2026-06-11 14:01:00] pair_scan_progress=50000/100000 ( 50.0%) elapsed=60.2s rate=830.1/s ok=41200 low_cell=7000 fail=1800
```

Suppress progress:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes ... --no-progress
```

Control progress frequency:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes ... --progress-every-pct 2 --progress-every-rows 5000
```

The `50_run_new_tool_mds.sh` runner saves these printed messages using `tee` into:

```text
pair_mds_gwes_spydrpick/logs/latest.log
```


## Command-line plotter

After `pip install .`, the plotting command is installed as:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes-plot \
  --input results/pair_mds_logistic.tsv \
  --out results/pair_distance_score.png
```

This is a Python console wrapper around the packaged R script, so it requires `Rscript` in `PATH`.

Install R dependencies once:

```r
install.packages(c("ggplot2", "data.table"))
```

Highlight a known pair:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes-plot \
  --input results/pair_mds_logistic.tsv \
  --out results/pair_distance_score.png \
  --highlight-pair 50000,90000 \
  --threshold 5
```

Write top hits:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes-plot \
  --input results/pair_mds_logistic.tsv \
  --out results/pair_distance_score.png \
  --top-out results/top_pairs.tsv \
  --top-n 100
```


## Previous-tool-style plotting

`pair-mds-gwes-plot` now follows the previous plotting scheme:

- grey: all background candidate pairs
- green: high-confidence selected rows
- orange: high-score non-OK/suspicious rows
- red: known/real epistasis rows from block files or `--highlight-pair`

Example:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes-plot \
  --score results/pair_mds_logistic.tsv \
  --out results/pair_mds_gwes.plot.png \
  --top-min-y 5 \
  --suspicious-min-y 5 \
  --ld-dist 10000 \
  --inblock results/true_snp_blocks \
  --true-block-ids 0,1,2,3,4 \
  --pair-mode all
```

If no `--top` file is supplied, high-confidence rows are selected from the score file using `--top-min-y` and `--top-n`.

To highlight only the D/E pair in an ABCDE benchmark:

```bash
pair-mds-gwes-plot \
  --score results/pair_mds_logistic.tsv \
  --out results/pair_mds_gwes.DE.png \
  --inblock results/true_snp_blocks \
  --true-block-ids 0,1,2,3,4 \
  --pair-mode de
```
